4.83.m:
Beyond that is Kāleśvara sacred ford, supreme and most excellent, O hero;
neither the age of Kali nor time torments the best of men who has bathed there.
Right there is Aśokatīrtha, far more auspicious even than that,
bathing where a man never falls into the ocean of sorrow.
Even purer than that, O prince, is Śukratīrtha,
bathing where the best of men is not born through semen.
Even more merit-bestowing than that, O king, is the excellent Bhavānītīrtha,
bathing where and beholding Bhavānī and Īśa, one does not exist again [in rebirth].
Renowned beyond that is Prabhāsatīrtha, auspicious for men;
in front of Someśvara, one who bathes there does not partake of a womb.
Beyond that is Garuḍatīrtha, destroying the poison of saṃsāra;
having worshipped Garuḍeśa and bathed there, one does not grieve.
Beyond that is the meritorious Brahmatīrtha in front of Vīrabrahmeśvara;
a man attains the knowledge of Brahman by bathing there.
Beyond that is Vṛddhārkatīrtha, and higher than that is Vidhitīrtha;
